**How to implement.** Every constructor window registers under its kit, so a second choice of the kit brings it forward (001 §E 'one window per kit'; step 190's registry key; step 180: `KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn` shows the window of a mode over an opened kit). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn` (step 180), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3, opens the window of the mode through `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory that builds `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` or `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)`, `context.settings.selectWindowModality` and `BrowseOpen`, under `opened.folder.windowKey` (steps 184, 190): `Ok (CreatedWindow _)` is the open; `Ok (ActivatedWindow _)` or `Ok (RetargetedWindow _)`, a window that already holds the kit, closes the opened kit again (`opened.library.kit.close ()`, step 131) so the one window keeps the kit; and `Error (WindowFactoryFailedErr (_, reason))` closes the opened kit and is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying the reason, as `openKitAt` logs a failed close (step 150). The registry forgets the window when it closes (`WindowLauncher.fs:225`), so the kit opens again after Close kit. No other code changes. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, with trait `ui-smoke`, through the start screen as step 180's facts go: `acceptance: choosing a kit whose window is open activates that window and opens no second one`: Main's start screen over a picker answering a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton`, opens one `MainConstructorWindow`; Inverse's start screen over a picker answering the same folder, pressing `openKitButton`, opens no constructor window and closes the screen, and the folder's `.oc/lock` still names this process; the same happens through a picker answering that folder written with backslashes and in upper case. `a kit can be opened again once its window is closed`: once that window is closed, Main's start screen pressing `openKitButton` over the folder opens one `MainConstructorWindow`. Each fact closes the windows it opened, so no registry key outlives it.

**Acceptance.** After the windows register, choosing a kit whose constructor window is open MUST bring that window forward, open no second one and keep its lock, and a closed window's kit MUST open again; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: choosing a kit whose window is open activates that window and opens no second one` and `a kit can be opened again once its window is closed`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
